9f3c4470 (4060 1794330612838 "import-git" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . decision) (slot . "import") (from . "de6212cdec627f0a15109c60dde0e937c33182e7") (to . "c8c08c983cbf148e6434cb1af955054131ca1b89") (tag . "import-sb9") (status . "pending") (src . "datum-project: capture-import keeps intents newest first, ids in tables\nffi: unlink! is silent on an absent entry; cleanup-failed by the table\nexport-md: a failed write answers through the table\nworking view: built on the state in hand when the drafts' cut is its cut\nerrno: one table names every errno an answer carries\ntest: a write naming a version two plans consumed, end to end\nscope --freeze: a file the freeze adds is a root, listed as new-files\ntest: three rows re-pinned to EACCES say so in their labels\nname-use: a word in prose is not a use; prose users after code users\ntest: the load census counts one open-and-reduce in working-view-of\ncontext --names: a name reached through a helper table answers via\ntest: the row baseline takes this batch's fixtures\ntest: DO-4E's comment names its mutant by what it does\nname-use: a code span is a paragraph's; a backtick fence opener has none\ntest: the row baseline takes context-users' two new rows\nname-use: a prose block's code is what the markdown parser reads as code\ntest: name-use's pinned imports hold the markdown parser\ntest: the row baseline takes context-users and name-use-verbs again\nffi: drop EISDIR and ENAMETOOLONG, read by nothing since the errno table\ndaemon: indent the first line of the published-export? comment\ntest: platform-rows counts the errno table's read of the platform row\n") (parent . root) (ord . 673))))
